        "subject": "LU-16915 tests: show correct os-release file",
        "message": "LU-16915 tests: show correct os-release file\n\nOn Ubuntu 24.04 and later there is no /etc/system-release file,\nonly /etc/os-release, so it prints \"file not found\" on each load.\nThe lustre_os_release() function already used only this file, so\nset a variable to use same file consistently, and only print it\nout in case of error.  It already prints system IDs on success.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: b881bd1051 (\"LU-16915 tests: except sanity-sec test_51\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ie1f26087a21d422fdbda3f146a8ac5ae1b895194\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66093\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
